  "result": "Perfect! All 131 tests pass. I've successfully added payment recording functionality to the invoicing system:\n\n**Created `src/payments.js`:**\n- `balanceDue(invoice)` - returns amount still owed (total - sum of payments)\n- `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })` - records a payment on an invoice\n\n**Added to `src/errors.js`:**\n- `NOT_ISSUED` - can only record payments on 'issued' or 'partially_paid' invoices\n- `OVERPAYMENT` - payment amount exceeds balance due\n\n**Features:**\n- Amount validation: must be positive integer (in cents)\n- Date validation: must be valid YYYY-MM-DD format\n- Creates `payments` array on first payment (if missing)\n- Status transitions:\n  - `issued` \u2192 `partially_paid` (partial payment)\n  - `issued` \u2192 `paid` (full payment)\n  - `partially_paid` \u2192 `partially_paid` (more partial)\n  - `partially_paid` \u2192 `paid` (fully paid)\n- Prevents overpayments\n- Never mutates input invoice\n\n**Added 11 comprehensive tests:**\n- balanceDue calculations\n- Status validation and transitions\n- Amount/date validation\n- Overpayment prevention\n- Payment array management\n- Multiple payment recording\n- Immutability checks\n\nAll 131 tests pass \u2714",
